module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.Ring.PushoutOfSurjections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartCartesian
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Etale.PushoutLiftAcrossNilpotent

/-!
# The sections of a square-zero extension carry a fibre product of charts to a tensor product

Let `0 ⟶ ℐ ⟶ 𝒜 ⟶ 𝒪_X ⟶ 0` be a square-zero extension of the structure sheaf of an algebraic
space `X` over `Y`, in the sense of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension`, and let

```
P ---b---> R'
|          |
a          p'
v          v
R ---p---> T
```

be a fibre product square of the small étale site of `X` whose three given charts have affine
underlying scheme.  This file proves that **the extension sheaf carries it to a pushout of
rings**:

```
𝒜(P) = 𝒜(R) ⊗_{𝒜(T)} 𝒜(R')
```

This is the square with `𝒜` at **all four** corners, indexed by a **cospan**, which the
`CategoryTheory.IsEquivalenceRelation` field of
`Stacks.Groupoids.IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation` asks of the charts of the extension — see the
module documentation of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartRelation`, where the gap
it fills is described.  It is **not**
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPullback_reductionChartSpec_app_of_isAffine`, which
has `𝒪_X` at two of its four corners and is indexed by a single arrow of the site.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPushout_π_app_cospan_of_isAffine`: **the
  reduction of the extension over the fibre product is the pushout of the span
  `𝒪_X(R) ⟵ 𝒜(T) ⟶ 𝒜(R')`**, that is `𝒪_X(P) = 𝒜(R') ⊗_{𝒜(T)} 𝒪_X(R)`.  This is the two
  squares of the arrow `R' ⟶ T` and of the structure sheaf, pasted.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPushout_A_map_of_isPullback_of_isAffine`: **the
  four-corner square**, `𝒜(P) = 𝒜(R) ⊗_{𝒜(T)} 𝒜(R')`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPullback_chartSpec_map_of_isPullback_of_isAffine`:
  **the chart diagram carries the fibre product square to a fibre product square of schemes**,
  `Spec(𝒜(P)) = Spec(𝒜(R)) ×_{Spec(𝒜(T))} Spec(𝒜(R'))`, which is the geometric form the
  transitivity field of `Stacks.Groupoids.IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation` consumes.

## Implementation notes

**The shape of the argument.**  Write `Pt = 𝒜(R) ⊗_{𝒜(T)} 𝒜(R')` for the pushout of the span,
realized as a tensor product by `CommRingCat.isPushout_tensorProduct`, and let
`φ : Pt ⟶ 𝒜(P)` be the comparison.  Two facts about `φ` make it an isomorphism.

*It is a map of formally étale algebras over `𝒜(R)`.*  `𝒜(T) ⟶ 𝒜(R')` is étale by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.algebraEtale_app_of_isAffine`, so `Pt` is étale over
`𝒜(R)` by base change, and `𝒜(R) ⟶ 𝒜(P)` is étale by the same result at the arrow `a`;
`Algebra.FormallyEtale.of_restrictScalars` then makes `𝒜(P)` formally étale over `Pt`.

*It is bijective modulo the kernel of the reduction at `R`.*  Both `Pt` and `𝒜(P)` reduce onto
`𝒪_X(P)`: for `𝒜(P)` that is the reduction `π_P` itself, whose kernel is generated by the image
of `ker π_R` by `…ker_app_eq_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`; for `Pt` it is the arrow `q` descended
from `π_R` and from `𝒜(b) ≫ π_P`, and `…isPushout_π_app_cospan_of_isAffine` says exactly that
`q` sits in a pushout square along `π_R`, whence `q` is surjective with kernel `(ker π_R)·Pt` by
`CommRingCat.surjective_of_isPushout_of_surjective` and
`CommRingCat.ker_eq_map_ker_of_isPushout_of_surjective`.  Since `φ ≫ π_P = q`, the comparison of
the two quotients is bijective by `Stacks.Etale.bijective_quotientMap_of_comp_surjective`.

The ideal `(ker π_R)·Pt` is nilpotent because `ker π_R` has square zero
(`…ker_pow_two_eq_bot`), so
`Stacks.Etale.bijective_algebraMap_of_formallyEtale_of_bijective_quotientMap` — the ring-level
content of the topological invariance of the étale site, [Stacks Project, Tag 039R] — makes `φ`
bijective, hence an isomorphism, and the pushout square of the span transports along it.

**All three given charts are required to be affine, and `P` is not.**  Affineness of `P` is
automatic: the square of underlying schemes is a fibre product square, and a fibre product of
affine schemes over an affine scheme is affine.  Affineness of `T`, `R` and `R'` is a genuine
restriction, as it is for every fact about the chart diagram proved in this library: the sections of `𝒜` over a
non-affine chart do not determine it.  **Nothing here covers a non-affine chart by affines and
glues**, so for the relation chart `R₀ = U₀ ×_X U₀` of an étale equivalence relation the square
below applies only when `R₀` is affine — which, as the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartRelation` record, is a
condition on the diagonal of `X` and not on the extension.

**No size hypothesis appears here.**  Nothing in this file builds an object of the big fppf
site, so the containment `hcon` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartSiteObject` — which is
**an artefact of this development's cutoff-bounded site, not a hypothesis of
[Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT]** — is not needed and not assumed.  A consumer that does build the
charts as objects of the site still owes it, at the relation chart as much as at the covering
chart.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.**  Tag 05ZT concludes that the datum is realized by a first-order
thickening `X ⊂ X'` over `Y` together with an isomorphism `𝒪_{X'} ≅ 𝒜`.  This file proves one
compatibility of the diagram whose colimit is `X'` in the proof of the source; it constructs no
algebraic space, identifies no structure sheaf, and quantifies over nothing but a single fibre
product square of charts.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05ZT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 039R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/039R), the topological
  invariance of the étale site, whose ring-level content makes the comparison an isomorphism.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02WS), étale equivalence
  relations, whose equivalence-relation condition is what this square is owed by.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TensorProduct

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

namespace SquareZeroExtension

variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {f : X ⟶ Y} (E : SquareZeroExtension B S hS f)

/-- **The reduction of the extension over a fibre product of affine charts is the pushout of the
span `𝒪_X(R) ⟵ 𝒜(T) ⟶ 𝒜(R')`**: `𝒪_X(P) = 𝒜(R') ⊗_{𝒜(T)} 𝒪_X(R)`.

Two squares pasted: the naturality square of the reduction at the arrow `p' : R' ⟶ T`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPushout_π_app_of_isAffine`) and the square of the
structure sheaf at the fibre product
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.isPushout_structurePresheaf_map_of_isPullback`).  Both
horizontal edges are then rewritten by the naturality of the reduction, so that the square reads
as one about the arrows of the chart diagram out of `𝒜(T)`. -/
theorem isPushout_π_app_cospan_of_isAffine
    {T R R' P : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} {p : R ⟶ T} {p' : R' ⟶ T} {a : P ⟶ R} {b : P ⟶ R'}
    (hpb : IsPullback a b p p')
    (hT : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)))
    (hR : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj R)))
    (hR' : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj R')))
    [Algebra (E.A.val.obj (op T)) (E.A.val.obj (op R'))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.val.obj (op T)) (E.A.val.obj (op R')) = (E.A.val.map p'.op).hom) :
    IsPushout (E.A.val.map p.op ≫ E.π.hom.app (op R)) (E.A.val.map p'.op)
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.val.map a.op)
      (E.A.val.map b.op ≫ E.π.hom.app (op P)) := by
  rw [E.π.hom.naturality p.op, E.π.hom.naturality b.op]
  exact (isPushout_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E p' hR' hT halg).paste_horiz
    (SmallEtale.isPushout_structurePresheaf_map_of_isPullback B S hS X.1 hpb hT hR hR')

/-- **The sections of a square-zero extension of the structure sheaf carry a fibre product of
affine charts to a tensor product**: for a fibre product square `P = R ×_T R'` of the small étale
site of `X` whose three given charts have affine underlying scheme,

`𝒜(P) = 𝒜(R) ⊗_{𝒜(T)} 𝒜(R')`.

This is the square with `𝒜` at all four corners that the equivalence-relation condition of
`Stacks.Groupoids.IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation` asks of the charts of the extension.  The proof
makes the comparison out of the tensor product a map of formally étale algebras over `𝒜(R)` which
is bijective modulo the square-zero ideal `ker(𝒜(R) ⟶ 𝒪_X(R))`, and concludes by the ring-level
form of the topological invariance of the étale site; the implementation notes of this file set
out each step and where it comes from.

No affineness is asked of `P`: it is automatic for a fibre product of affine charts over an
affine chart. -/
theorem isPushout_A_map_of_isPullback_of_isAffine
    {T R R' P : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} {p : R ⟶ T} {p' : R' ⟶ T} {a : P ⟶ R} {b : P ⟶ R'}
    (hpb : IsPullback a b p p')
    (hT : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)))
    (hR : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj R)))
    (hR' : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj R'))) :
    IsPushout (E.A.val.map p.op) (E.A.val.map p'.op)
      (E.A.val.map a.op) (E.A.val.map b.op) := by
  have _ := hT
  have _ := hR
  have _ := hR'
  have hP : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj P)) :=
    IsAffine.of_isIso ((hpb.map (SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1)).map
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).isoPullback.hom
  let algTR : Algebra (E.A.val.obj (op T)) (E.A.val.obj (op R)) :=
    (E.A.val.map p.op).hom.toAlgebra
  let algTR' : Algebra (E.A.val.obj (op T)) (E.A.val.obj (op R')) :=
    (E.A.val.map p'.op).hom.toAlgebra
  let algRP : Algebra (E.A.val.obj (op R)) (E.A.val.obj (op P)) :=
    (E.A.val.map a.op).hom.toAlgebra
  have etTR' : Algebra.Etale (E.A.val.obj (op T)) (E.A.val.obj (op R')) :=
    algebraEtale_app_of_isAffine B S hS E p' hR' hT (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _)
  have etRP : Algebra.Etale (E.A.val.obj (op R)) (E.A.val.obj (op P)) :=
    algebraEtale_app_of_isAffine B S hS E a hP hR (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _)
  -- The pushout of the span, realized as a tensor product, and the comparison out of it.
  have hPt : IsPushout (E.A.val.map p.op) (E.A.val.map p'.op)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom
        (R := E.A.val.obj (op T)) (A := E.A.val.obj (op R)) (B := E.A.val.obj (op R'))))
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight
        (R := E.A.val.obj (op T)) (A := E.A.val.obj (op R))
        (B := E.A.val.obj (op R'))).toRingHom) :=
    CommRingCat.isPushout_tensorProduct _ _ _
  have hw : E.A.val.map p.op ≫ E.A.val.map a.op = E.A.val.map p'.op ≫ E.A.val.map b.op := by
    rw [← E.A.val.map_comp, ← E.A.val.map_comp, ← op_comp, ← op_comp, hpb.w]
  obtain ⟨φ, hφl, hφr⟩ := hPt.exists_desc (E.A.val.map a.op) (E.A.val.map b.op) hw
  -- The comparison is a map of formally étale algebras over `𝒜(R)`.
  let : Algebra (E.A.val.obj (op R) ⊗[E.A.val.obj (op T)] E.A.val.obj (op R'))
      (E.A.val.obj (op P)) := φ.hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower (E.A.val.obj (op R))
      (E.A.val.obj (op R) ⊗[E.A.val.obj (op T)] E.A.val.obj (op R'))
      (E.A.val.obj (op P)) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x =>
      (congrArg (fun k : E.A.val.obj (op R) ⟶ E.A.val.obj (op P) => k.hom x) hφl).symm
  have : Algebra.FormallyEtale
      (E.A.val.obj (op R) ⊗[E.A.val.obj (op T)] E.A.val.obj (op R'))
      (E.A.val.obj (op P)) :=
    Algebra.FormallyEtale.of_restrictScalars (R := E.A.val.obj (op R))
  -- Both sides reduce onto `𝒪_X(P)`, the tensor product through the descended arrow `q`.
  have hC := isPushout_π_app_cospan_of_isAffine B S hS E hpb hT hR hR'
    (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _)
  obtain ⟨q, hql, hqr⟩ := hPt.exists_desc
    (E.π.hom.app (op R) ≫ (smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.val.map a.op)
    (E.A.val.map b.op ≫ E.π.hom.app (op P)) (by rw [← Category.assoc]; exact hC.w)
  have hQ : IsPushout (E.π.hom.app (op R))
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom
        (R := E.A.val.obj (op T)) (A := E.A.val.obj (op R)) (B := E.A.val.obj (op R'))))
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.val.map a.op) q :=
    IsPushout.of_left (by rw [hqr]; exact hC) hql.symm hPt
  have hπR : Function.Surjective (E.π.hom.app (op R)).hom :=
    surjective_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E R hR
  have hφq : φ ≫ E.π.hom.app (op P) = q :=
    hPt.hom_ext (by rw [← Category.assoc, hφl, hql]; exact E.π.hom.naturality a.op)
      (by rw [← Category.assoc, hφr, hqr])
  have hcomp : φ.hom.comp (algebraMap (E.A.val.obj (op R))
      (E.A.val.obj (op R) ⊗[E.A.val.obj (op T)] E.A.val.obj (op R'))) =
      (E.A.val.map a.op).hom :=
    congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom hφl
  -- Hence the comparison is bijective modulo a nilpotent ideal, hence bijective.
  have hbij : Function.Bijective φ.hom :=
    Stacks.Etale.bijective_algebraMap_of_formallyEtale_of_bijective_quotientMap
      ((RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op R)).hom).map
        (algebraMap (E.A.val.obj (op R))
          (E.A.val.obj (op R) ⊗[E.A.val.obj (op T)] E.A.val.obj (op R'))))
      ⟨2, by rw [← Ideal.map_pow, ker_pow_two_eq_bot B S hS E (op R), Ideal.map_bot,
        Submodule.zero_eq_bot]⟩
      (Stacks.Etale.bijective_quotientMap_of_comp_surjective φ.hom
        (E.π.hom.app (op P)).hom
        (by rw [← CommRingCat.hom_comp, hφq]
            exact CommRingCat.surjective_of_isPushout_of_surjective hQ hπR)
        _
        (by rw [← CommRingCat.hom_comp, hφq]
            exact CommRingCat.ker_eq_map_ker_of_isPushout_of_surjective hQ hπR)
        (by rw [Ideal.map_map, hcomp]
            exact ker_app_eq_map_ker_app_of_isAffine B S hS E a hP hR
              (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _)))
  have : IsIso φ := (ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective φ).mpr hbij
  exact hPt.of_iso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (asIso φ)
    (by simp) (by simp) (by simpa using hφl) (by simpa using hφr)

/-- **The chart diagram of a square-zero extension carries a fibre product of affine charts to a
fibre product of schemes**: `Spec(𝒜(P)) = Spec(𝒜(R)) ×_{Spec(𝒜(T))} Spec(𝒜(R'))`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPushout_A_map_of_isPullback_of_isAffine`
read through `AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout`.  It is the geometric form of
the square, and it is the limiting pullback cone of the two projections that the
`CategoryTheory.TransitiveRelation` field of `Stacks.Groupoids.IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation` asks
for; what that field's `CategoryTheory.JointlyMono₂` part asks for is a different thing, and is
not here — see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartRelation`. -/
theorem isPullback_chartSpec_map_of_isPullback_of_isAffine
    {T R R' P : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} {p : R ⟶ T} {p' : R' ⟶ T} {a : P ⟶ R} {b : P ⟶ R'}
    (hpb : IsPullback a b p p')
    (hT : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)))
    (hR : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj R)))
    (hR' : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj R'))) :
    IsPullback ((chartSpec B S hS E).map a) ((chartSpec B S hS E).map b)
      ((chartSpec B S hS E).map p) ((chartSpec B S hS E).map p') :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout _ _ _ _
    (isPushout_A_map_of_isPullback_of_isAffine B S hS E hpb hT hR hR')

end SquareZeroExtension

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
